course: dictionary
lesson: 13350
title: The big toe and the hallux
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The hallux is the scientific name for your big toe. It is the first and largest toe on your foot. «The nurse checked Mia's hallux after she stubbed it on the bed.» Here the word means the big toe, so picture the toe at the front of your foot.
explain: Birds have a hallux too, but it is in a different place. In a bird, the hallux is the toe that points backwards. «The parrot gripped the branch with its hallux.» That backward toe helps the bird hold on when it perches.
explain: Words like hallux often come from Latin, the old language that scientists use for names. When you meet one, read the words around it. Ask: is this talking about a foot or a bird? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Hallux» means the big toe.
fact: The hallux is the first and largest toe of the foot.
fact: In birds, the hallux is the toe that points backwards.
fact: The hallux helps birds grip branches when they perch.
fact: Doctors use hallux in words like «hallux valgus», which is another name for a bunion.
exercise: «The nurse checked Mia's hallux after she stubbed it.» What does hallux mean? | *The big toe | The ankle | The heel | The little toe
exercise: In birds, which toe is the hallux? | The toe that points forwards | *The toe that points backwards | The longest feather | The toe on the wing
exercise: Dr Patel says, «You have hallux valgus.» What is another name for hallux valgus? | A cold in the foot | *A bunion | A broken toenail | A blister on the heel
test: «The hallux of the bird gripped the branch tightly.» Which toe is this? | The wing feather | *The backward-pointing toe of a bird | The big toe of a foot | The tail
test: What is the plural of hallux? | *Halluces | Hallus | Hallux-es | Halluxes
exam: A bird uses its hallux to hold on. What does the hallux help a bird do? | Swim underwater | Fly high | Sing loudly | *Grip a branch when perching
